+
+
+### Guild Hall letter badges removed; live quest-result popups now queue instead of dropping simultaneous completions (patch 0289)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Patch 0289
+- Changed: the single-letter badge on every Guild Hall facility/upgrade card is gone (Barracks/Treasury/Workshop/Library/etc.) -- just the card now
+- Fixed: when several heroes' quests finished in the exact same moment (Send All Idle's own favorite trick), only the last one got a reward pop-up -- every other completion in that batch is now shown too, one after another, instead of being silently skipped
+```
+
+**Guild Hall letter badges.** Direct request with a screenshot circling the small boxed letter (B/T/W/L/etc.) on every Facilities card. Traced to `UpgradeCard` (GuildPanel.tsx) -- a single shared component behind both the Facilities grid and the Permanent Upgrades grid (`facilityCard`/`generalUpgradeCard` both render through it), rendering `<div className="guild-facility-icon">{name.charAt(0)}</div>` ahead of the card's own title/body. Removed the div outright (`name` itself is still used for the actual title text just below it, untouched) and the now-dead `.guild-facility-icon` CSS rule alongside it -- confirmed via grep it wasn't referenced anywhere else. `.guild-facility-card`'s flex layout needed no adjustment: the body was already `flex: 1`, so it simply fills the space the icon used to occupy; the shared `gap: 12px` between flex children is a no-op with only one child left.
+
+**Live quest-result pop-up -- asked whether one exists, then found it silently drops completions.** Confirmed one already exists: `QuestResultModal`/`QuestResultCard` reads `engine.lastResult` (a `QuestResult` set the moment a quest resolves during live play) and shows a count-up gold/xp card with loot, gated by the "Quest result pop-ups" toggle in Settings > Quality of life (on by default). While tracing how `lastResult` gets set to answer the question fully, found it was a bare field, not a queue -- every call site (the live tick loop, and the DevTool's `testCompleteActiveQuest`/`testCompleteAllActiveQuests`) just did `this.lastResult = result;` directly. A single tick's `due` loop can resolve more than one hero's quest at once -- routine after Send All Idle sends several heroes out together on the same duration -- and each resolution in that loop overwrote the previous one before React ever got a chance to render it, so only the LAST hero in that batch ever actually got a pop-up; every earlier completion in the same tick was silently and invisibly dropped, no error, nothing in the log.
+
+**Fixed with a small FIFO queue, not a rewrite.** New private `GameEngine.queuedResults: QuestResult[]` (transient, unsaved -- same "genuinely ephemeral" treatment `lastResult` itself already gets, explicitly not persisted). New `pushResult(result)` replaces every direct `this.lastResult = result` assignment: shows immediately if nothing's currently displayed (byte-identical to the old behavior for the single-completion case, the overwhelmingly common one), otherwise queues behind whatever's already showing. `dismissResult()` now drains the queue -- `this.lastResult = this.queuedResults.shift() ?? null` -- instead of just nulling out, so the next queued completion takes over the instant the player dismisses the current card, in the order they actually finished. `QuestResultCard` itself needed zero changes: it already keys off `result.questId` and re-mounts fresh per result, so handing it a new queued result through the exact same `lastResult` prop it already reads just works. `hardReset()` (new-guild wipe) also clears `queuedResults` alongside `lastResult`, so a fresh guild never inherits a stale queue from the guild it replaced.
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean against a fresh clone with this patch applied. No `SAVE_VERSION` bump needed -- `queuedResults` is in-memory GameEngine state, not `GameState`, same as `lastResult` it sits beside. Worth a real playtest: send several heroes out at once on the same duration (Send All Idle onto freshly-refreshed boards is the easiest repro), let them all land in the same tick, and confirm every one of them gets its own reward card in turn rather than only the last.
